Please don't just say "Reality has no place in NetHack" because that 
simply isn't true. Some of my favourite moments in learning to play 
NetHack have been finding out just how much reality they have crammed 
in. I fondly remember when I discovered you could put towels on your 
head, or that you could go fishing with a bullwhip, or that if a god 
aims a bolt of lightning at you while you are swallowed it will hit the 
swallower instead.

Perhaps "intuition" is a better word than "reality". But since our 
intuition is based on reality, what difference does it make?

Within this debate, I think it would be logical for missile damage to be 
proportional to range - so a rock from a sling would go further and do 
more damage than a thrown rock. However, I think the current system, 
despite defying physics, is intuitive enough.

